  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fairtrade Partnerships</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The DFAT Fairtrade ANZ Partnership (Phase 2) seeks to foster the sustainable livelihoods of small-scale producers and their communities through enabling fair terms of trade. Building on current producer support programs, the project leverages the existing experience of Fairtrade ANZ to benefit additional communities. The project is assisting producer associations to develop linkages with international processors, traders and manufacturers and build their capacity to manage the financial, business and governance aspects of the association. Producer support activities will enable farmers to meet the quality and volume standards required to meet certification standards and better access international markets. The project also seeks to increase consumer awareness of the Fairtrade label and develop commercial partnership and co-investment.</narrative>
  </description>
